  "slug": "my-marriage",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/6368_my-marriage.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "When we first got married, I was just an ordinary doctor, and my husband was a middle school teacher. Our daily life was very regular. After we got up every morning, we would have breakfast together, watch the news, and then go to work together. We lived a very happy life. Ten years have passed, and now he is the principal and I have become the director of the hospital. Our positions are getting higher and higher, and our work is getting busier and busier. I can't see him when I get up every morning. When I go home at night, he is already asleep. We have fewer and fewer opportunities to eat and communicate together. When we meet occasionally, we don’t know what to say anymore. I once hoped that we could have fewer meetings, more rest, and be together as often as before, but no one was willing to give up their careers, so in the end we had no choice but to divorce."
  ],
  "english_full": "When we first got married, I was just an ordinary doctor, and my husband was a middle school teacher. Our daily life was very regular. After we got up every morning, we would have breakfast together, watch the news, and then go to work together. We lived a very happy life. Ten years have passed, and now he is the principal and I have become the director of the hospital. Our positions are getting higher and higher, and our work is getting busier and busier. I can't see him when I get up every morning. When I go home at night, he is already asleep. We have fewer and fewer opportunities to eat and communicate together. When we meet occasionally, we don’t know what to say anymore. I once hoped that we could have fewer meetings, more rest, and be together as often as before, but no one was willing to give up their careers, so in the end we had no choice but to divorce.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "Когда́ мы пе́рвый раз пожени́лись, я бы́ла простóй до́ктор и мой муж бы́л наста́вником в сре́дней шко́ле. Наша ежедне́вная жизнь бы́ла о́чень обыкнове́нной. По́сле того́ как мы поднима́лись ка́ждое у́тро, мы завтрака́ли вме́сте, смотри́ли ве́сти, а затем идём на рабо́ту вме́сте. Мы жили о́чень сча́стливой жизнью."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Kogdá my pérrvyy raz pozhénilis', ya býla prostóy dóktor i moy múzh býl nastávnikom v srédenyey shkéle. Nasha yezhédnevnaya zhizn' býla óchyen' obyknovénnoy. Pósle togó kak my podnimális' kázhdoye útro, my zavtrakáli vméste, smotrílí vésti, a zátém idyóm na rabótu vméste. My zhili óchyen' schástlivoy zhizn' ."
  ],
